# 📄 **SystemRules.md (Expanded + Ultra‑Detailed)**

```markdown
# System Rules — EH Graced Roads Solutions LLC (Enterprise Edition)

## 1. NO‑TOW Policy (Absolute Rule)

> WE DO NOT PROVIDE TOW SERVICE OR WINCHING SERVICE.

### Enforcement:
- No tow vendors  
- No tow yard routing  
- No tow‑related UI  
- No tow‑related backend endpoints  
- No tow‑related AI outputs  
- No tow‑related documentation  

This rule overrides all other logic.

---

## 2. Emergency Protocol Rules

- Emergency protocol must follow all 11 steps in order.  
- No skipping hazard scan or diagnosis.  
- Technician dispatch must be repair‑focused.  
- Vendor selection must be repair‑only.  
- After‑hours workflow must use repair networks.  
- Grace must log every step.  
- Frontend must visualize protocol progress.  

---

## 3. GPS Pipeline Rules

- All units must be trackable.  
- GPS updates must be validated.  
- Grace must use GPS for routing.  
- Frontend must update maps in real time.  
- GPS data must be stored historically.  

---

## 4. UI Rules

- Dual‑monitor layout is mandatory.  
- Monitor 1 = breakdowns + dispatch.  
- Monitor 2 = GPS + routing.  
- System health indicators must be visible.  
- NO‑TOW banner must appear in emergency views.  

---

## 5. Backend Rules

- All routes must enforce NO‑TOW policy.  
- All emergency routes must call Grace.  
- All GPS routes must validate input.  
- All critical actions must be logged.  
- All Socket.IO events must be documented.  

---

## 6. AI Rules

- AI must use `/docs` as the single source of truth.  
- AI must enforce NO‑TOW policy.  
- AI must generate repair‑only workflows.  
- AI must maintain brand voice.  
- AI must follow architecture.  
- AI must follow emergency protocol.  

---

## 7. Security Rules

- Role‑based access (dispatcher, technician, admin).  
- Logging of critical actions.  
- No external tow integrations.  
- No unauthorized vendor suggestions.  

---

## 8. Documentation Rules

- All changes must be reflected in `/docs`.  
- All workflows must be documented.  
- All modules must have architecture notes.  
- All UI components must have mockup references.  
```

